<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alghero</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as L'Alguer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alghero is a port on the north-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Taken by the Crown of Aragon in 1354 and resettled with Catalans, it has kept a Catalan dialect, still spoken by part of its population, and Catalan Gothic buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alghero.jpg" alt="Alghero" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gianni Careddu · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alghero_-_Panorama_(02).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The conquests of James I spread the Catalan language and settlers to Valencia and the Balearic Islands, and the Catalan dialect of <b>Alghero</b> in Sardinia survives today.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The royal towns, above all Cagliari, Sassari, <b>Alghero</b>, Iglesias and Oristano, enjoyed charters and their own councils.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Through that expansion Catalan language and law reached Valencia, the Balearic Islands and the town of <b>Alghero</b> in Sardinia, where a Catalan dialect is still spoken.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Off <b>Alghero</b> in northwestern Sardinia, the allied fleet of the Crown of Aragon and the Republic of Venice crushed the fleet of the Republic of Genoa, capturing most of it.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-27">27 August in history</a></li></ul></section>
